  "notes": [
    "Batch 1 (pilot), labelled by the agent (Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code) on 2026-11-23, before any Ward check, analyzer or MCP tool existed. Karlo reviews the bar and spot-checks cases before step 02.",
    "Candidates came from repository security advisories of Android apps and from GitHub commit and PR search (keywords: security, CVE, GHSA, vulnerability, exported, cleartext, traversal, allowBackup, setWebContentsDebuggingEnabled), committed after 2026-06-30. Each case links where it was found.",
    "Every fix is newer than both models' training cutoff (June 2026), so neither model can have seen it.",
    "The flawed version is the parent commit; the fix commit is that case's clean twin. Line numbers refer to the parent commit. No code from the repos is stored: only URLs, hashes, paths, lines, short anchors and our own words.",
    "Rejected while labelling: thunderbird-android 016baf0421 ('OkHttp patch for CVE-2026-11943'): that CVE is an unrelated web app and OSV lists no advisory for OkHttp 5.5.0. frostwire 256db2b14e (netty-all 4.2.19 bump): its own message says the fixed advisories are unconfirmed, and OSV lists none for 4.2.19.",
    "Batch 2 candidates (not labelled): signalapp/Signal-Android b60f53f4df (zip-slip via dot-only chat names), duckduckgo/Android 6eff8db71b (JS bridge origin taken from a pending navigation), element-hq/element-x-android GHSA-r4f9-46vw-v7g3 (crash via malformed OIDC intent).",
    "HO-07 has no exact MASWE weakness (credentials sent to a look-alike host); MASWE-0050 is the closest. Scoring accepts the MASVS control.",
    "Dependency checks: HO-04's advisories were confirmed with an OSV query for com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.20.1 on 2026-11-23."
  ],
